.SH "NAME"
econf\&.ReadConfig, econf\&.ReadConfigWithCallback \- evaluate configuration files for a specific project

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
import "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/go/econf"
.fi
.ft
.sp
.nf
\fBfunc ReadConfig(project, usrSubdir, configName, configSuffix, delim, comment string) (*econf\&.File, error)\fR

\fBfunc ReadConfigWithCallback(project, usrSubdir, configName, configSuffix, delim, comment string, callback econf\&.FileCallback) (*econf\&.File, error)\fR
.fi

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
\fBReadConfig\fR
evaluates key/values of a given configuration by reading and merging all
needed/available files from different directories\&. Order is:\&

   /etc/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR does exist:

     * /etc/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
     * \fIusrSubdir\fR/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
     * /run/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
     * /etc/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR

   /etc/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR does NOT exist:

     /run/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR does exist:

       * /run/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
       * \fIusrSubdir\fR/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
       * /run/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
       * /etc/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR

     /run/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR does NOT exist:

       * \fIusrSubdir\fR/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
       * \fIusrSubdir\fR/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
       * /run/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
       * /etc/\fIproject\fR/\fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR

   No main \fIconfigName\fR\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR file is defined or must not be parsed:

     * \fIusrSubdir\fR/\fIproject\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
     * /run/\fIproject\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR
     * /etc/\fIproject\fR\&.d/*\&.\fIconfigSuffix\fR

.PP
\fIproject\fR
is the name of the project used as subdirectory, and may be
""
(treated as
NULL
by the underlying C call)\&.

.PP
If
\fIconfigName\fR
is
""\&, drop\-ins without a main configuration file will be parsed only\&.
\fIconfigSuffix\fR
may also be
""\&.

.PP
The
\fIdelim\fR
parameter specifies the character used to separate keys from values (e\&.g\&.,
"="
)\&. If
\fIdelim\fR
contains space characters AND non\-space characters, multiline values are
not parseable\&. The
\fIcomment\fR
parameter specifies an array of characters which define the start of a
comment (e\&.g\&.,
"#"
)\&.

.PP
\fBReadConfigWithCallback\fR
behaves like
\fBReadConfig\fR, additionally invoking
\fIcallback\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_FileCallback\fR(3)) for every candidate file before it is
parsed\&. Returning
\fIfalse\fR
from
\fIcallback\fR
aborts the read, and the call fails with
\fBeconf\&.ErrParsingCallbackFailed\fR\&.

.PP
The returned
\fI*File\fR
should be released with
\fB(*File)\&.Close\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_File_Close\fR(3)) once it is no longer needed\&.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
On success, these functions return a non\-nil
\fI*econf\&.File\fR
holding the merged configuration, and a
\fInil\fR
error\&.

.PP
On failure, they return
\fInil\fR
and a non\-nil
\fI*econf\&.Error\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_Error\fR(3))\&.

.SH "ERRORS"

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoFile\fR
.RS 4
          No matching configuration file could be found\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoMem\fR
.RS 4
          Insufficient memory to allocate the resulting
\fBeconf\&.File\fR\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrMissingBracket\fR, \fBeconf\&.ErrTextAfterSection\fR, \fBeconf\&.ErrEmptySectionName\fR, \fBeconf\&.ErrMissingDelimiter\fR
.RS 4
          A file contains syntax errors and could not be parsed successfully\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrArgumentIsNullValue\fR
.RS 4
          One of the required arguments is empty when it must not be\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrParsingCallbackFailed\fR
.RS 4
          \fBReadConfigWithCallback\fR
only: the callback returned
\fIfalse\fR
for one of the candidate files\&.
.RE

.SH "EXAMPLE"

Reading content in different cases in following order:\&

   /etc/foo/example\&.conf does exist:

     * /etc/foo/example\&.conf
     * /usr/lib/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
     * /run/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
     * /etc/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf

   /etc/foo/example\&.conf does NOT exist:

     /run/foo/example\&.conf does exist:

       * /run/foo/example\&.conf
       * /usr/lib/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
       * /run/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
       * /etc/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf

     /run/foo/example\&.conf does NOT exist:

       * /usr/lib/foo/example\&.conf
       * /usr/lib/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
       * /run/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
       * /etc/foo/example\&.conf\&.d/*\&.conf
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 1
.\}
.nf

package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "log"

    "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/go/econf"
)

func main() {
    conf, err := econf\&.ReadConfig(
        "foo",        // project name
        "/usr/lib",   // vendor directory
        "example",    // config name
        "conf",       // suffix
        "=",          // delimiter
        "#")          // comment
    if err != nil {
        log\&.Fatal(err)
    }
    defer conf\&.Close()

    value, err := conf\&.String("main", "greeting")
    if err != nil {
        log\&.Fatal(err)
    }
    fmt\&.Println(value)
}

.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

